From: CBOC-Vita <344212538+CBOC-Vita@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:26:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 78/79] io: a read cache and read-ahead worker for the disc
 image, reads straight into guest memory, UMD read-ahead hints honoured

IsoReadCache (kernel/iso_read_cache.hpp): aligned 64 KiB blocks (about 8 MB, least recently used out first), a handle of its own on the
file, and a worker thread that reads blocks ahead of a sequential reader (four slots of streams) and where the game's UMD read-ahead
command (sceIoDevctl 0x01F300A5) says it will read. The bytes are the file's. Every read of the source goes through one local mutex, always taken before the port's stdio lock
(a wrapped fopen in reopen), never after it, so the two cannot deadlock; stab's notify_resumed() drives IsoImage::reopen(). A failed read is retried once after the source was opened
again (IsoImage::reopen() / IsoReadCache::reopen() for a wake from sleep); a block that could not be read is never cached. Reads of
1 MiB or more skip the cache. The worker starts through IoThreadPlatform (core and priority), std::thread by default.

read_file_op reads a disc read into guest memory directly when the range is one piece of it (no vector, no second copy).

<prefix>_IO_CACHE=0 reads as before; _IO_CACHE_MB (8), _IO_CACHE_AHEAD (4 blocks), _IO_CACHE_WORKER=0. iso_cache_stats() gives
hits, misses, waits, prefetched, errors for the platform's status line.

tests/iso_read_cache_tests.cpp: random and concurrent reads equal direct reads, the end of the image, a truncated source, a failing
source with reopen and retry, hints, eviction, and IsoImage on a synthetic ISO 9660 file.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
